// Exact int8 Tensor Core GEMM: C[64][32] = A[64][128] * B[32][128]^T
//
// `mma.sync.m16n8k32.row.col.s32.s8.s8.s32` accumulates int8 products into an
// int32 accumulator EXACTLY, so the reduction is associative and the result
// does not depend on how K was split across warps, CTAs or launches. That is
// the GPU half of what docs/deterministic_inference.md M0 established on the
// CPU.
//
// B is [N][K], not [K][N] — that is what `.col` means for this instruction,
// and it is the natural layout for an inference weight matrix. Passing a
// [K][N] buffer computes a different function with no diagnostic.
@tile(64, 32, 128)
kernel int8_gemm(A: GlobalMemory<I8>, B: GlobalMemory<I8>, C: GlobalMemory<I32>) {
}

